    en: "Djebel Onk Phosphate Mine is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Algeria. The largest phosphate deposit in Algeria, crucial for the fertilizer industry and export. Huge reserves. Processed in Annaba. Important for agriculture. This location plays a role in the economy of Algeria, strongly shaped by oil and natural gas extraction. Like many notable places in Algeria, it combines Berber heritage with Mediterranean and Saharan influences. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Algeria."
